
========================================================================
P1  Classical braid-arrangement control
========================================================================
n=2: Poincare=[1, 1]; top=1=1
n=3: Poincare=[1, 3, 2]; top=2=2
n=4: Poincare=[1, 6, 11, 6]; top=6=6
n=5: Poincare=[1, 10, 35, 50, 24]; top=24=24
n=6: Poincare=[1, 15, 85, 225, 274, 120]; top=120=120
n=7: Poincare=[1, 21, 175, 735, 1624, 1764, 720]; top=720=720
Scope: this is cohomology of one braid complement, not an invariant of each tournament.

========================================================================
P2  Classical finite-field braid and Shi controls
========================================================================
n=3, q=11: braid=990; Shi=704
n=3, q=13: braid=1716; Shi=1300
n=4, q=11: braid=7920; Shi=3773
n=4, q=13: braid=17160; Shi=9477
Scope: these textbook point counts do not identify Shi walls with LRC safety walls.

========================================================================
P3  Minimal witness: a thickened safe set is not a standard toric complement
========================================================================
S={1}, delta=1/5: |G_delta|=3/5
ordinary complement of ker(z -> z) in the circle: Haar measure=1
Therefore |G_delta| is not ordinary toric-complement volume.

========================================================================
P4  Exact signed phase-height wall arithmetic
========================================================================
self pair v=1: |det((v,+1),(v,-1))|=2
self pair v=2: |det((v,+1),(v,-1))|=4
self pair v=3: |det((v,+1),(v,-1))|=6
v=1, w=2: same-sign=1=|v-w|; opposite-sign=3=v+w
v=1, w=3: same-sign=2=|v-w|; opposite-sign=4=v+w
v=2, w=3: same-sign=1=|v-w|; opposite-sign=5=v+w
Full-torus determinants expose pair-sum arithmetic; the top-slope proof selects the ruler.

========================================================================
P5  Finite B=2 scout and a hostile standard-toric control
========================================================================
hard-coded universe: 72 primitive triples; unique B=2 leader=(4, (1, 2, 3))
natural circle hypertori union: (1,2,3) has 4 points; (2,3,4) has 6
Thus the B=2 relation count is not Betti/Mobius mass and is cutoff-dependent.

========================================================================
SUMMARY
========================================================================
Classical braid/Shi formulas survive.  THM-1820's Fourier annihilator identity survives.
The live LRC arrangement is the labelled, oriented phase-height cell complex for
X_S={(v,+1),(v,-1)} with its selected inequality side and height functional.
Ordinary complement cohomology is not known to recover the selected state;
abstract relation lattices and bounded B=2 relation data are provably lossy.
